om/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T20:28:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T20:28:28Z","body":"> Can you test if it happens in 4.5.2? To eliminate any cherry picked fixes in that\n\nIt does happen in 4.5.2.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138005376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4139059692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117852#issuecomment-4139059692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117852","id":4139059692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72tQns","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T23:47:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T00:02:07Z","body":"I'm able to reproduce this in 4.4.1, 4.5, 4.5.1, 4.5.2 and latest `master`. I don't think this is a regression, which would make sense, since the relevant code hasn't changed since 4.4.\n\nI would not personally say that this is a bug with the Jolt implementation (other than there being a discrepancy with Godot Physics) but rather with the fact that we indiscriminately call `Node3D::set_global_transform` during the `RigidBody3D` state synchronization, regardless of whether the body's transform has actually changed or not:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/babc272d44ecfbd86e3b3fc5397ef936b1ce12d8/scene/3d/physics/rigid_body_3d.cpp#L149-L152\n\nThis will always dirty the transforms and cause a transform update/notification throughout that entire node branch.\n\nThis applies to Godot Physics as well, if you enable contact reporting on the body. It also technically applies when leaving the body as non-frozen (and non-sleeping) and then letting it sit perfectly still, but the simulation will likely jiggle the body ever so slightly in that case anyway.\n\nI would prefer to keep the current behavior as far as state synchronization goes, so I would say the fix in this case is to just add a transform comparison to `RigidBody3D::_sync_body_state`, and maybe the other nodes that use `body_set_state_sync_callback` as well.\n\n@MajorMcDoom I'm a little bit curious as to why you need `can_sleep` disabled on a kinematic body to begin with. What's the use-case exactly?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4139059692/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4139283704","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117852#issuecomment-4139283704","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117852","id":4139283704,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72uHT4","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:51:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T00:53:08Z","body":"> I'm able to reproduce this in 4.4.1, 4.5, 4.5.1, 4.5.2 and latest `master`. I don't think this is a regression, which would make sense, since the relevant code hasn't changed since 4.4.\n\nYou're right, I just tried it again, and was able to repro in 4.5.1, which for some reason I was not able to do yesterday. Must have been a mistake on my part. Thanks for confirming. I've edited the bug report to reflect the correct repro versions.\n\n> I would prefer to keep the current behavior as far as state synchronization goes, so I would say the fix in this case is to just add a transform comparison to `RigidBody3D::_sync_body_state`, and maybe the other nodes that use `body_set_state_sync_callback` as well.\n\nI agree it's the right fix. Granted, a transform comparison has a small cost, but I think it's necessary if you consider behavioural consistency, and it's a single-point cost against potentially much greater cascading costs of the entire hierarchy receiving the notification.\n\n> [@MajorMcDoom](https://github.com/MajorMcDoom) I'm a little bit curious as to why you need `can_sleep` disabled on a kinematic body to begin with. What's the use-case exactly?\n\nIt's not that I need a frozen body to not fall asleep. It's that I have normally unsleepable dynamic bodies that _can be frozen_. The use case is that I need complete predictability of when my objects are at rest, instead of letting the physics engine decide.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4139283704/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]